<title>BRAZIL: Brazil govt to auction 149,705 bags coffee July 16.</title>
<headline>Brazil govt to auction 149,705 bags coffee July 16.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's government is to auction 149,705 60-kg bags of coffee from its stocks at a regular monthly auction on July 8, said a statement from Banco do Brasil, which is to hold the electronic sale.</p>
<p>Members of the domestic roasting and soluble coffee industry as well as exporters can participate in the auction.</p>
<p>The monthly sale had originally been scheduled to take place on July 2 but had been postponed to allow for the official publication of an extension in the payment terms to 120 days.</p>
<p>Details of the coffees included in the auction are as follows. Quantity is in bags:  </p>
<p>    QTY	CROP	COLOR	LOCATION		     TYPE</p>
<p> 22,890   1986/87   Yellowish   Conceicao Rio Verde, MG    6</p>
<p> 10,000   1987/88   Yellowish   Juiz de Fora, MG	     6</p>
<p> 12,300   1987/88   Greenish    Cianorte, PR		   6</p>
<p> 24,900   1987/88   Yellowish   Loanda, PR		   6/7</p>
<p> 13,150   1987/88   Whitish     Rolandia, PR		 6/7</p>
<p> 10,264   1987/88   Yellowish   Rolandia, PR		   7</p>
<p> 10,000   1987/88   Light green Ribeirao Pinhal, PR	  6</p>
<p> 25,868   1987/88   Yellowish   St Cruz Rio Pardo, SP	6</p>
<p>  6,998   1987/88   Yellowish   Catanduva, SP		  6</p>
<p>  2,966   1987/88   Yellowish   Catanduva, SP		  6</p>
<p> 10,369   1987/88   Yellowish   Lins, SP			 6</p>
<p>TOTAL - 149,705 bags</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
